[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 1. Endless stdin: the Rust program hung where the C program exits
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Symptom** — `yes 1.5 | driver`: the C program prints
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `3ff8000000000000 0x1.8p+0 1.5000` and exits 0 immediately; the Rust program
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   never terminated (killed by a 3 s timeout, status 124, no output).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Cause** — `main` did `stdin().read_to_end(&mut input)` and only then
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   parsed. `scanf` does the opposite: it consumes bytes one at a time, stops at
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the first byte that cannot extend the conversion, and never waits for EOF.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Against a producer that does not close the pipe, reading to EOF cannot
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   return. The same bug also made memory use proportional to the whole stream
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   rather than to the token.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Fix** — `src/main.rs`: added `struct Input<R: Read>`, a lazily-filled view
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   of the stream with random access by absolute index (`at(i)` returns `None`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   only at true end of stream, and pulls another chunk only when asked for an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   index it has not reached). `scan_double`, `scan_hex`, `scan_decimal` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `ci_prefix_len` now index through it instead of through a `&[u8]` slurped up
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   front. The parsing logic is otherwise unchanged: `i < len && input[i] == X`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   became `input.matches(i, X)`, `i >= len` became `input.at(i).is_none()`, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   so on.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Regression test** — `endless_stdin_terminates_like_the_c_program`. Feeds
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `"1.5\n"` for ever from a helper thread and polls `try_wait` against a 20 s
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   deadline. Verified to fail (`did not terminate on an endless stdin`) when the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `read_to_end` version is put back.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 2. Closed stdout: the Rust program exited 0 where the C program dies from SIGPIPE
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Symptom** — with stdout a pipe whose reader has already gone away
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`printf 1.5 | driver | true`), the C program is killed by `SIGPIPE`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (shell status 141, signal 13); the Rust program exited 0.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Cause** — the Rust runtime sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN` before `main` runs,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   so the failing write returns `EPIPE` instead of raising a signal. The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   previous code then discarded that `io::Result` (`let _ = write!(...)`) and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   fell off the end of `main` with status 0. The C program runs with the default
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   disposition and is terminated by the signal.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Fix** — `src/main.rs`: `restore_default_sigpipe()`, called first in `main`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   puts `SIGPIPE` back to `SIG_DFL` via a direct `extern "C" fn signal`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   declaration (no new dependency; libc is already linked). Discarding the write
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   result is now correct, because the process dies before the result is seen —
